<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47792" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tentātor</span></b> , ōris,
			m.
		tento. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>An assailant</i>, <i>attempter</i>,
				<i>tempter</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">integrae Dianae (Orion),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 3, 4, 71</span></i>
			.—Esp., <i>the tempter</i>, i. e. <i>the devil</i>, <i><span class="en">Vulg. Matt. 4,
				3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Juvenc. 1,
			384</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>He who attacks</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">autumnus, tentator valetudinum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Anim. 48 <i>init.</i></span></i>
			</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
